      "content": "\"neurotargeting\"... that's exactly the word. it feels so predatory. if they're actually using \"thinking design\" to bypass our logic, then it's not even marketing anymore, it's just psychological hacking. i've been noticing it more in the way the whole campaign feels synchronized across different platforms, like it's a coordinated strike on our dopamine receptors. can you look into the specific psychological mechanics of how that exact shade of blue combined with those specific geometric angles could be used to induce a trance-like state or a compulsive urge to consume? i need to know if there's any actual science that supports this kind of predatory optimization.",
